docs/USER_MANUAL.md:472:| `/copy [diff\|code\|last]` | Copy diff, code blocks, or response to system clipboard. With no clipboard tool (`wl-copy`, `xclip`, `xsel`, `pbcopy`: SSH, tmux, headless) the live TUI asks the terminal to copy it with an OSC 52 request instead (up to 74,994 bytes; larger text is refused, never cut). The terminal does not confirm it: terminals may ignore OSC 52, tmux needs `set -g set-clipboard on`, GNU screen is not supported. The text reaches the terminal only base64-encoded, after the same credential redaction and control-character handling as every sidecar message. `NEXUS_OSC52=off` (also `0`, `false`, `no`, `none`) turns the fallback off, and the older line-mode REPL does not use it. |
