docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md:18:On a terminal, running `nexus` with no arguments opens the live TUI; in non-interactive pipes or via `nexus repl`, it opens the interactive REPL. Non-interactive tasks require the explicit `run` subcommand (`nexus run "<task>"`). Unknown subcommands exit non-zero with an error (REQ-REL-104). The interactive slash commands include `/help`, `/status`, `/doctor`, `/mode`, `/compact`, `/clear`, `/resume`, `/sessions`, `/save`, `/export [md|json]`, `/checkpoints`, `/undo`, `/git`, and `/exit`. Availability and usage are listed by `/help` in the running client. `nexus run` supports JSON results with `--json`; its execution, verification outcome, and acceptance are separate. `VERIFIED` means the selected verifier ran and passed; a model saying it is done is not verification.
